  run_ids: ["6a39faa6-e685-4b93-891d-df53c89e2ba8"] -> ["55195973-3064-4000-92c5-408679c6864d"]
  explanation: "Extraction caveat: the twenty-four primitive models were produced with pinned Charon's --preset aeneas --monomorphize combination, which its options explicitly declare incompatible. A preset-validation-order defect admitted it. Lean checks the stated generated-model theorems, but their Rust-to-model correspondence is conditional on this unsupported extraction path; a supported re-extraction is under review. The three generic slice bodies use separate non-monomorphic extraction and retain their callback premises. Independent Kani checks of primitive valid-index behavior and layouts are separate evidence. The unchanged bit_field 0.10.3 single-bit methods are verified for all twelve integer types: in-range indices read or update exactly that bit, returned mutable-reference writes propagate to the original value, and invalid indices fail at the assertion. All twelve primitive BIT_LENGTH values equal their widths. The original generic slice bit_length/get_bit/set_bit bodies are also composition-proved: assuming their declared BitField constant and per-element normal-return contracts, they use element index bit/width and local index bit%width, preserve other slice entries on update, and report zero-width/out-of-bounds errors. bit_length returns length times width or integerOverflow. Rust source and Cargo.toml are archive-identical." -> "The unchanged bit_field 0.10.3 single-bit methods are verified for all twelve integer types: in-range indices read or update exactly that bit, returned mutable-reference writes propagate to the original value, and invalid indices fail at the assertion. All twelve primitive BIT_LENGTH values equal their widths. The original generic slice bit_length/get_bit/set_bit bodies are also composition-proved: assuming their declared BitField constant and per-element normal-return contracts, they use element index bit/width and local index bit%width, preserve other slice entries on update, and report zero-width/out-of-bounds errors. bit_length returns length times width or integerOverflow. Rust source and Cargo.toml are archive-identical."
  trusted_assumptions: "The official Rust/Charon/Aeneas translation and integer/slice models, Lean, and Kani/CBMC are trusted. Twelve explicit monomorphized size_of models supply the integer byte sizes on x86_64, including pointer size 8; Kani checks their actual layouts and all primitive single-bit methods/returned-reference behavior for arbitrary valid values. Connecting Kani Rust and Lean representations is a reviewed bridge, not an in-Lean std layout proof; Rust nightlies differ. Generic slice theorems assume the complete stated observation/update callback contracts, including the final state after returned-reference writeback. They do not prove arbitrary callback implementations. Mapped audits allow only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. The primitive extraction caveat concerns Charon 08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f: options.rs678-688 rejects full monomorphization with Aeneas lowering choices, but main.rs211-218 validates before driver.rs233 applies the preset. The known upstream fix f679421a5946296f1f6628dcb67907bafece2639 repairs validation order, not support for that combination. No unconditional Rust correspondence follows from the affected generated-model theorems alone. The selected primitive IR was structurally audited: no dangling function references, indexing/array/reference-unsizing operations or corresponding known failure pattern were found; its direct calls refer to declared size and initialization functions. No defect was detected in these selected bodies. This audit does not make the frontend option combination officially supported." -> "The official Rust/Charon/Aeneas translation and integer/slice models, Lean, and Kani/CBMC are trusted. The size_of model uses Lean-only PrimitiveRustLayout evidence with twelve supplied primitive instances, including pointer size8 on x86_64. The original generated Funs is unchanged: each of its twelve ground calls statically elaborates to the expected instance dictionary, checked explicitly. This added implicit evidence is not a Rust trait or an in-Lean proof of std layout. The Lean class remains extensible; coverage is the frozen twelve-call closure, not class sealing. Bool lacks an instance in the audited environment, and there is no supplied fallback for arbitrary types. Kani checks the same twelve actual layouts and all primitive single-bit/returned-reference behavior for arbitrary valid values. Connecting Kani Rust and Lean representations is a reviewed bridge, not an in-Lean std layout proof; Rust nightlies differ. Generic slice theorems assume the complete stated observation/update callback contracts, including the final state after returned-reference writeback. They do not prove arbitrary callback implementations. Mapped audits allow only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound."
  environment: "Original crates.io bit_field0.10.3; x86_64 default features, debug extraction. Rust nightly-2026-09-17, Charon08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f, Aeneas be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a, Lean4.35.0. Official original-body extraction with primitive monomorphization and separate generic slice roots. Kani0.68.0/CBMC6.11.0/Rust nightly-2026-08-21: 24 supplementary primitive harnesses/600 checks, plus the separate concrete range observation." -> "Original crates.io bit_field0.10.3; x86_64 default features, debug extraction. Rust nightly-2026-09-17, Charon08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f, Aeneas be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a, Lean4.35.0. Official non-monomorphizing Aeneas-preset extraction for primitive roots and separate generic slice roots. The prior unsupported monomorphize/preset snapshot is retained as labeled evidence; all current contracts are rechecked from the supported path. Kani0.68.0/CBMC6.11.0/Rust nightly-2026-08-21: 24 supplementary primitive harnesses/600 checks, plus the separate concrete range observation."
