  "trusted_assumptions": "The official Rust/Charon/Aeneas translation and integer/slice models, Lean, and Kani/CBMC are trusted. The size_of model uses Lean-only PrimitiveRustLayout evidence with twelve supplied primitive instances, including pointer size8 on x86_64. The original generated Funs is unchanged: each of its twelve ground calls statically elaborates to the expected instance dictionary, checked explicitly. This added implicit evidence is not a Rust trait or an in-Lean proof of std layout. The Lean class remains extensible; coverage is the frozen twelve-call closure, not class sealing. Bool lacks an instance in the audited environment, and there is no supplied fallback for arbitrary types. Kani checks the same twelve actual layouts and all primitive single-bit/returned-reference behavior for arbitrary valid values. Connecting Kani Rust and Lean representations is a reviewed bridge, not an in-Lean std layout proof; Rust nightlies differ. Generic slice theorems assume the complete stated observation/update callback contracts, including the final state after returned-reference writeback. They do not prove arbitrary callback implementations. Mapped audits allow only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.",
